,15,87,12,19,20,19732,59,37018,220,17,45340,61,17,12,16,15,87,12,21,24,51185,15,7110,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nFind the positive solution to\n\\[\\frac 1{x^2-10x-29}+\\frac1{x^2-10x-45}-\\frac 2{x^2-10x-69}=0.\\]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"8415990e98f9feccdbf6d04d680a31d7bb742ed8298c94d849d3cd2fed7ae8a7"},"seconds":42.83035612106323,"seed":454994502434846879,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the given equation\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{x^2-10x-29} + \\frac{1}{x^2-10x-45} - \\frac{2}{x^2-10x-69} = 0,\n\\]\nwe start by letting \\( y = x^2 - 10x - 29 \\). Then the equation transforms into\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{y-16} - \\frac{2}{y-40} = 0.\n\\]\nNext, we find a common denominator for the fractions, which is \\( y(y-16)(y-40) \\). Rewriting the equation with this common denominator, we get\n\\[\n\\frac{(y-16)(y-40) + y(y-40) - 2y(y-16)}{y(y-16)(y-40)} = 0.\n\\]\nThe numerator must be zero, so we focus on the numerator:\n\\[\n(y-16)(y-40) + y(y-40) - 2y(y-16) = 0.\n\\]\nExpanding each term, we have\n\\[\n(y^2 - 56y + 640) + (y^2 - 40y) - (2y^2 - 32y) = 0,\n\\]\nwhich simplifies to\n\\[\ny^2 - 56y + 640 + y^2 - 40y - 2y^2 + 32y = 0,\n\\]\nand further simplifies to\n\\[\n-64y + 640 = 0.\n\\]\nSolving for \\( y \\), we get\n\\[\n-64y = -640 \\implies y = 10.\n\\]\nRecall that \\( y = x^2 - 10x - 29 \\), so we substitute \\( y = 10 \\) back into this equation:\n\\[\nx^2 - 10x - 29 = 10 \\implies x^2 - 10x - 39 = 0.\n\\]\nWe solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\( x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\), where \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = -10 \\), and \\( c = -39 \\). Substituting these values in, we get\n\\[\nx = \\frac{10 \\pm \\sqrt{100 + 156}}{2} = \\frac{10 \\pm \\sqrt{256}}{2} = \\frac{10 \\pm 16}{2}.\n\\]\nThis gives us two solutions:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{26}{2} = 13 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x = \\frac{-6}{2} = -3.\n\\]\nSince we are asked to find the positive solution, we have\n\\[\n\\boxed{13}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{13}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
